---
import AsterLayout from "../../layouts/AsterLayout.astro";
import { ASTER_DEX_ID, AUTHORS, PERSON_ID, SITE_URL } from "../../entity";
import { buildAsterPageGraph, buildBreadcrumbs } from "../../lib/schema";
import { ASTER_DOCS, ASTER_LAST_VERIFIED } from "../../data/aster";

const url = `${SITE_URL}/aster-dex/tax-reporting/`;
const description =
  "How to reconstruct Aster DEX activity for tax reporting: perp PnL, funding, staking rewards, airdrops, bridges and the records most traders forget.";

const articleNode = {
  "@type": "TechArticle",
  "@id": `${url}#article`,
  headline: "Tax reporting",
  alternativeHeadline: "Reconstructing Aster DEX activity for tax reporting",
  name: "Reconstructing Aster DEX activity for tax reporting",
  description,
  url,
  mainEntityOfPage: url,
  inLanguage: "en",
  datePublished: "2026-11-24",
  dateModified: ASTER_LAST_VERIFIED,
  author: { "@id": AUTHORS.kirsty.id },
  editor: { "@id": AUTHORS.maksim.id },
  publisher: { "@id": PERSON_ID },
  isPartOf: { "@id": `${SITE_URL}/aster-dex/#collection` },
  articleSection: "Tax",
  about: [
    { "@id": ASTER_DEX_ID },
    { "@type": "Thing", name: "Tax", sameAs: "https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q8161" },
    { "@type": "Thing", name: "Capital gain", sameAs: "https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q1850816" },
  ],
  citation: [
    { "@type": "CreativeWork", name: "Aster API documentation", url: `${ASTER_DOCS}for-developers/aster-api/api-documentation` },
    { "@type": "CreativeWork", name: "Aster terms: taxes", url: `${ASTER_DOCS}resources/terms-and-conditions` },
  ],
};

const breadcrumbs = buildBreadcrumbs(`${url}#breadcrumbs`, [
  { name: "Home", url: `${SITE_URL}/` },
  { name: "Aster DEX", url: `${SITE_URL}/aster-dex/` },
  { name: "Tax reporting", url },
]);

const graph = buildAsterPageGraph([articleNode, breadcrumbs]);
---

<AsterLayout
  title="Aster DEX Tax Reporting — Records, PnL and Common Gaps | Maksim Sokal"
  description={description}
  canonical={url}
  graph={graph}
  trail={[{ label: "Tax reporting" }]}
  modified={new Date(ASTER_LAST_VERIFIED)}
>
  <header class="space-y-5 max-w-3xl">
    <span class="text-xs font-mono text-sky-400 uppercase tracking-widest block">Tax</span>
    <h1 class="font-display font-medium text-3xl md:text-4xl text-slate-100 tracking-tight leading-tight">
      Tax reporting
    </h1>
    <p class="text-sm text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
      DEX activity is harder to report than exchange activity because there is no single statement. Perp closes,
      funding, staking rewards, airdrops, bridges and LP positions each create a different record. This page is about
      reconstructing those records correctly — not about a specific country's rates.
    </p>
    <p class="text-[11px] font-mono text-slate-400">
      Updated <time datetime={ASTER_LAST_VERIFIED}>{ASTER_LAST_VERIFIED}</time> · not tax advice
    </p>
  </header>

  <section class="bg-amber-500/5 border border-amber-400/20 rounded-xl p-5 space-y-2" aria-label="Tax disclaimer">
    <p class="text-[11px] font-mono uppercase tracking-widest text-amber-200">Scope</p>
    <p class="text-xs text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
      Tax treatment depends on your residence, citizenship and the character of the activity. Nothing here is tax,
      legal or accounting advice. Use it as a checklist for the data you need, then confirm the treatment with a
      qualified professional in your jurisdiction.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="space-y-3" aria-labelledby="events-heading">
    <h2 id="events-heading" class="font-display font-medium text-xl text-slate-100 tracking-tight">The events to capture</h2>
    <ul class="space-y-2 text-xs text-slate-400 leading-relaxed list-disc pl-5">
      <li><strong class="text-slate-300">Perp opens and closes</strong> — realised PnL on close, plus fees.</li>
      <li><strong class="text-slate-300">Funding payments</strong> — income or expense depending on direction and jurisdiction.</li>
      <li><strong class="text-slate-300">Trading fees</strong> — often deductible against gains, but only if recorded.</li>
      <li><strong class="text-slate-300">Staking and Earn rewards</strong> — asBNB NAV growth, USDF/asUSDF distributions, ALP NAV changes.</li>
      <li><strong class="text-slate-300">Airdrops</strong> — usually income at receipt, with a cost basis for later disposal.</li>
      <li><strong class="text-slate-300">Bridges</strong> — often not a disposal, but the transfer must be tracked to preserve basis.</li>
      <li><strong class="text-slate-300">Liquidations</strong> — realised loss plus the liquidation fee.</li>
      <li><strong class="text-slate-300">Referral commissions</strong> — income in most jurisdictions.</li>
      <li><strong class="text-slate-300">Token swaps</strong> — including USDT–USDC and small-asset conversions.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="space-y-4" aria-labelledby="sources-heading">
    <h2 id="sources-heading" class="font-display font-medium text-xl text-slate-100 tracking-tight">Where the data lives</h2>
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-4">
      <div class="bg-brand-900/35 border border-[#1e293b]/60 rounded-xl p-5 space-y-2">
        <h3 class="font-display text-sm text-slate-100">Aster account</h3>
        <p class="text-xs text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">Trade history, funding, fees and positions. Export or query before closing the account.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="bg-brand-900/35 border border-[#1e293b]/60 rounded-xl p-5 space-y-2">
        <h3 class="font-display text-sm text-slate-100">Aster API</h3>
        <p class="text-xs text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">For high-volume accounts, pulls fills and funding without manual exports. See the <a href="/aster-dex/api/" class="text-sky-400 hover:text-sky-300">API guide</a>.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="bg-brand-900/35 border border-[#1e293b]/60 rounded-xl p-5 space-y-2">
        <h3 class="font-display text-sm text-slate-100">Explorers</h3>
        <p class="text-xs text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">Deposits and withdrawals on BNB Chain, Ethereum, Arbitrum, Solana and SUI. Needed to tie the account back to the wallet.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="space-y-3" aria-labelledby="perps-heading">
    <h2 id="perps-heading" class="font-display font-medium text-xl text-slate-100 tracking-tight">Perpetuals: realised, not unrealised</h2>
    <p class="text-xs text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
      Opening a perp is usually not a disposal; closing it realises the PnL. The trap is treating an open position's
      unrealised gain as taxable, or forgetting that funding has been accruing the whole time. Reconstruct the position
      lifecycle: open, every funding payment, fees, partial closes, final close.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="space-y-3" aria-labelledby="yield-heading">
    <h2 id="yield-heading" class="font-display font-medium text-xl text-slate-100 tracking-tight">Earn products need a different treatment</h2>
    <p class="text-xs text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
      asBNB, asBTC and asUSDF accrue value into the token's net asset value rather than paying a separate dividend. That
      means the reward is embedded in the token price, and it becomes realised when you sell or redeem. ALP is a pool
      token whose NAV moves with profit and loss, so part of the change is yield and part is capital. Record the mint,
      the NAV at each reporting date, and the redemption separately.
    </p>
    <p class="text-xs text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
      asCAKE is in wind-down. Redemptions to CAKE after April 2025 are disposals and should be recorded like any other
      token swap.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="space-y-3" aria-labelledby="mistakes-heading">
    <h2 id="mistakes-heading" class="font-display font-medium text-xl text-slate-100 tracking-tight">Common gaps</h2>
    <ul class="space-y-2 text-xs text-slate-400 leading-relaxed list-disc pl-5">
      <li>Using only the exchange statement and missing on-chain deposits.</li>
      <li>Ignoring funding because it does not appear as a trade.</li>
      <li>Treating a bridge transfer as a disposal, or losing the original cost basis.</li>
      <li>Recording airdrops at zero cost and later overpaying tax on the full sale.</li>
      <li>Not recording fees, which are often the easiest deduction to support.</li>
      <li>Assuming one jurisdiction's wash-sale or loss rules apply everywhere.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="border-t border-[#1e293b]/60 pt-6 space-y-2">
    <p class="text-[11px] text-slate-400">
      Related: <a href="/aster-dex/api/" class="text-sky-400 hover:text-sky-300">API</a> ·
      <a href="/aster-dex/earn/" class="text-sky-400 hover:text-sky-300">Earn products</a> ·
      <a href="/aster-dex/eligibility/" class="text-sky-400 hover:text-sky-300">eligibility</a>
    </p>
    <p class="text-[11px] text-slate-400">
      Written by <a href="/kirsty-moreland/" class="text-sky-400 hover:text-sky-300">Kirsty Moreland</a> · Technical review by{" "}
      <a href="/about/" class="text-sky-400 hover:text-sky-300">Maksim Sokal</a> ·
      <a href="/disclosure/" class="text-slate-400 hover:text-sky-300">Disclosure</a>
    </p>
  </section>
</AsterLayout>
